+/*
+Kit 89 (R324, the owner 2026-11-18: "Debris stage by stage"; runs 90-96:
+the cascade's heavy half loses ~41% of its cycles to the I-cache, each of
+~110 debris pieces running the whole model path, lighting then bones then
+the emit, far past 32 KiB). Iterate (rule 0): GoldSrc and Xash light each
+model as it is drawn, interleaving the light code with the draw code per
+piece; ours runs the lighting stage for every model of the frame first,
+in one pass (R_DrawEntitiesOnList's start), so its code stays cached
+across all of them, and each model's draw takes the stored result. The
+same answer by construction: the result is used only when every input the
+function reads is bit for bit what the pass saw (the entity's origin,
+model, effects, render fx, the switches, the time, the world's light key
+and every dynamic light, which a model's own events may add while the
+frame draws); otherwise it is worked out anew. What the function writes
